# Windows Hardware Information API Reference

This skill documents native Windows interfaces for retrieving hardware information. 
All APIs listed are available on most Windows systems without additional driver 
or vendor SDK installations.

---

## CPU Information

### Static CPU Information

**`GetSystemInfo`** (`kernel32.dll`)

Retrieves hardware information including processor type, number of processors, 
page size, and OEM identifier.[reference:0]

```c
SYSTEM_INFO siSysInfo;
GetSystemInfo(&siSysInfo);
// siSysInfo.dwNumberOfProcessors - number of logical CPUs
// siSysInfo.dwProcessorType - processor architecture
```

GetLogicalProcessorInformationEx (kernel32.dll)

Retrieves detailed logical processor information, including core-to-logical 
processor mapping.

---

CPU Temperature (Limited Availability)

WMI Class: Win32_PerfFormattedData_Counters_ThermalZoneInformation

Available on some systems to retrieve thermal zone (CPU package) temperature. 
Requires administrator privileges. May not be populated on all hardware.

```powershell
Get-WmiObject -Query "SELECT * FROM Win32_PerfFormattedData_Counters_ThermalZoneInformation" -Namespace "root/CIMV2"
```

WMI Class: MSAcpi_ThermalZoneTemperature (root/wmi)

ACPI thermal zone sensor - returns CPU package approximate temperature. 
Requires administrator privileges. Not available on all systems.

---

Memory Information

System Memory Status

GlobalMemoryStatusEx (kernel32.dll)

Retrieves current physical and virtual memory usage information including 
total physical memory, available physical memory, memory load, and page file 
information.

```c
MEMORYSTATUSEX memStatus;
memStatus.dwLength = sizeof(MEMORYSTATUSEX);
GlobalMemoryStatusEx(&memStatus);
// memStatus.ullTotalPhys - total physical memory
// memStatus.ullAvailPhys - available physical memory
// memStatus.dwMemoryLoad - current memory load percentage
```

GetPerformanceInfo (psapi.dll)

Retrieves performance information including physical memory available, 
commit total, and commit limit.

---

Memory Performance Counters

WMI Performance Counter Classes (Win32_PerfFormattedData_*)

Pre-calculated performance counter data available through WMI.

Counter Class Description
Win32_PerfFormattedData_PerfOS_Memory System memory counters: Available Bytes, Committed Bytes, Page Faults/sec, Cache Bytes
Win32_PerfFormattedData_PerfProc_Process Per-process memory counters

PDH Performance Counters (pdh.dll)

Programmatic access to performance counters used by Perfmon.

Memory counters include: \Memory\Available Bytes, \Memory\Committed Bytes, 
\Memory\% Committed Bytes In Use

---

Disk Storage Information

Disk Space

GetDiskFreeSpaceEx (kernel32.dll)

Retrieves disk volume space information: total space, total free space, 
and free space available to the calling user.

```c
ULARGE_INTEGER available, total, free;
GetDiskFreeSpaceEx(L"C:\\", &available, &total, &free);
// total.QuadPart - total disk space in bytes
// free.QuadPart - total free space in bytes
```

---

Disk I/O Performance

WMI Class: Win32_PerfFormattedData_PerfDisk_PhysicalDisk

Physical disk performance counters including read/write bytes/sec, 
disk queue length, and disk time percentages.

Property Description
DiskReadBytesPerSec Bytes read per second
DiskWriteBytesPerSec Bytes written per second
DiskBytesPerSec Total bytes per second
CurrentDiskQueueLength Current queue length
PercentDiskTime Disk busy percentage

PDH Performance Counters (pdh.dll)

\PhysicalDisk(*)\Disk Read Bytes/sec
\PhysicalDisk(*)\Disk Write Bytes/sec
\PhysicalDisk(*)\% Disk Time

DeviceIoControl + IOCTL_DISK_PERFORMANCE

Retrieves raw disk performance statistics including read/write counts, 
byte counts, and time spent.

---

Network Adapter Information

Adapter Configuration

GetAdaptersInfo (iphlpapi.dll)

Retrieves IPv4 configuration information for all network adapters including 
adapter name, description, MAC address, IP address, subnet mask, gateway, 
and DHCP configuration.

```c
IP_ADAPTER_INFO adapterInfo[256];
ULONG bufferSize = sizeof(adapterInfo);
GetAdaptersInfo(adapterInfo, &bufferSize);
// Iterates through linked list of IP_ADAPTER_INFO structures
```

GetAdaptersAddresses (iphlpapi.dll)

Extended adapter information including both IPv4 and IPv6 addresses.

---

Network Performance

WMI Class: Win32_PerfRawData_Tcpip_NetworkInterface

Raw network interface performance counters including bytes sent/received 
per second.

Property Description
BytesReceivedPerSec Bytes received per second
BytesSentPerSec Bytes sent per second
BytesTotalPerSec Total bytes per second

WMI Class: Win32_PerfFormattedData_Tcpip_NetworkInterface

Pre-calculated network performance data.

PowerShell: Get-NetAdapterStatistics

Returns cumulative bytes sent and received for network adapters.

---

Graphics / GPU Information

Basic GPU Information

WMI Class: Win32_VideoController

Retrieves basic GPU information: name, adapter RAM, driver version. 
Does NOT provide temperature, utilization, or detailed VRAM usage.

```powershell
Get-WmiObject -Class Win32_VideoController | Select-Object Name, AdapterRAM
```

---

GPU Temperature and Performance

Windows does NOT provide a native, vendor-agnostic API for GPU temperature, 
utilization, or detailed VRAM usage. These require vendor-specific SDKs:

Vendor SDK/Interface DLL
NVIDIA NVML / NVAPI nvml.dll / nvapi64.dll
AMD ADL / ADLX atiadlxx.dll
Intel IGCL ControlLib.dll

DXCore (Windows 10+)

Provides some GPU information including adapter name and memory usage via 
AdapterMemoryUsageBytes. Temperature support is limited.

---

System Information

General System Information

GetSystemInfo (kernel32.dll)

Processor architecture, page size, minimum/maximum application address, 
and number of processors.

GetSystemMetrics (user32.dll)

Retrieves system metrics and configuration settings including display 
dimensions, scroll bar sizes, and system-wide UI metrics.

Index Description
SM_CXSCREEN Screen width in pixels
SM_CYSCREEN Screen height in pixels
SM_CXVIRTUALSCREEN Virtual screen width
SM_CYVIRTUALSCREEN Virtual screen height
SM_CMONITORS Number of monitors

---

API Classification

Category Interface Type Primary Use
CPU GetSystemInfo Win32 API Static hardware info
CPU Win32_PerfFormattedData_Counters_ThermalZoneInformation WMI Temperature (limited)
Memory GlobalMemoryStatusEx Win32 API RAM usage status
Memory GetPerformanceInfo Win32 API Performance metrics
Memory Win32_PerfFormattedData_PerfOS_Memory WMI Memory counters
Disk GetDiskFreeSpaceEx Win32 API Disk space info
Disk Win32_PerfFormattedData_PerfDisk_PhysicalDisk WMI Disk I/O counters
Network GetAdaptersInfo Win32 API Adapter configuration
Network Win32_PerfRawData_Tcpip_NetworkInterface WMI Network throughput
GPU Win32_VideoController WMI Basic GPU info only
GPU NVML/ADLX/IGCL Vendor SDK Temperature, utilization, VRAM
System GetSystemMetrics Win32 API Display/system metrics

---

Notes

· WMI performance counter classes are accessed via the root\cimv2 namespace.
· PDH (Performance Data Helper) provides programmatic access to the same 
  counters visible in Perfmon.
· Raw vs Formatted: Win32_PerfRawData_* classes provide raw counter values 
  requiring calculation; Win32_PerfFormattedData_* classes provide 
  pre-calculated values.
· GPU temperature and detailed VRAM usage are not available through standard 
  Windows APIs and require vendor-specific SDKs.
· CPU temperature via WMI may not be populated on all hardware and often 
  requires administrator privileges.